  "notes": "{黙|だま}る means to become silent or stop talking, often implying a deliberate choice to remain quiet.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{黙|だま}って⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ indicates the state of being silent or keeping quiet.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {黙|だま}った⟦まま→〜まま：02007_mama⟧: remaining silent, without speaking\n- {黙|だま}って + verb: silently doing something\n- {黙|だま}って⟦いて→いる：00495_iru⟧⟦ください→ください：02899_kudasai⟧: please be quiet\n- ⟦{黙|だま}りこむ→黙り込む：18270_damarikomu⟧: to fall into silence (compound verb)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {黙|だま}れ: Shut up! (imperative, rude)\n- ⟦{沈黙|ちんもく}→沈黙：13249_chinmoku⟧: silence (noun, formal)\n\nUSAGE:\n{黙|だま}って often implies doing something without asking permission or informing others: {黙|だま}って⟦{出|で}かける→出かける：00833_dekakeru⟧ (to leave without saying anything).",
